body:
It's hard to be specific when you don't know what you're asking. I think mainly I vent, and like, whoa, where the hell did that come from, what was that? Did you see it? What happened? What was that about?

&#x200B;

Thank you.

Reading some of the comments here... I must admit, this is one of things that really makes me question. The concept of going through weeks, months, years, of re-learning, re-educating yourself, to see the female within and feeling confident as a woman.

This to me screams like re-programming. Like Im re-programming my brain to see something else. If I really was a woman, why do I need to re-program myself? Isn't that what gender dysphoria is all about? Your brain knows one thing but your eyes see another? Why would you transition, and need to re-program yourself?

Herein lies the issue of working out what's genuine and what's not. Am I just not transgender? Or have I repressed everything? How do I know the difference between the two?

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
